      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Part 3 of 3: Record the decision and notify the employee\n**Employee Request and Approval Router**\n\n1. Is Approved?: checks the decision from the previous step and splits the workflow into two paths based on it.\n\n2. Mark Approved: if approved, updates that exact same row in the Data Table, setting its status to Approved and recording the time of the decision.\n\n3. Notify Employee - Approved: a placeholder for the moment. In a real build this emails the employee that they were approved. Swap in your own Gmail, Outlook, or Slack node here to actually send it.\n\n4. Mark Rejected: if declined instead, updates the same row with status Rejected and the time of the decision.\n\n5. Notify Employee - Declined: the same kind of placeholder, for letting the employee know their request was not approved this time.",
        "width": 760,
        "height": 360
      }
    }
